# Super Admin Customization Canvas Style

This rule documents the shared canvas-style preview used across super-admin customization pages so they match the hero-slider experience.

## Reference: Hero Slider

The hero-slider page ([frontend/src/app/(super-admin)/super-admin/settings/customization/hero-slider/page.tsx](frontend/src/app/(super-admin)/super-admin/settings/customization/hero-slider/page.tsx)) uses [TemplatePreview](frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/TemplatePreview.tsx), which defines the canvas pattern:

- **Outer section**: `rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4`
- **Header**: Title "پیش‌نمایش قالب" + optional device toggles / badge
- **Empty state**: Dashed border box, icon, title, description
- **Viewport**: `rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-3`
- **Browser frame**: Fake chrome (three dots + "infinitycolor.co" bar) + content area

## Shared Component: CustomizationPreviewSection

All non–hero-slider customization previews use [CustomizationPreviewSection](frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/CustomizationPreviewSection.tsx):

- **Props**: `title` (default "پیش‌نمایش قالب"), optional `badge`, optional `empty` (`EmptyStateConfig`: icon, title, description), `browserFrame` (default true), `children`
- **Exports**: `BrowserChrome` (reusable fake browser bar + content wrapper), `EmptyStateConfig` type
- Use `browserFrame` for a consistent “site preview” look; use `empty` when there is no data to show

## Pages Using the Canvas Style

| Page | Location | Preview component |
|------|----------|-------------------|
| Hero slider | hero-slider/page.tsx | TemplatePreview (reference; does not use CustomizationPreviewSection) |
| Featured category | featured-category/page.tsx | CustomizationPreviewSection + FeaturedCategoryPreviewInner |
| Home banners | home-banners/page.tsx | CustomizationPreviewSection + HomeBannersPreviewInner |
| Navbar | NavigationEditor | CustomizationPreviewSection + NavigationPreview |

## Adding a New Customization Preview

1. Build the preview content (e.g. a small component that renders from form/data).
2. Wrap it in `CustomizationPreviewSection` with `title="پیش‌نمایش قالب"`, `browserFrame`, and `empty` when the data set is empty.
3. Pass the wrapper as the `footer` of `UpsertPageContentWrapper` if the page uses the form + footer layout.

## Preview accuracy (match the real site)

To keep previews as accurate as the hero slider, customization previews reuse the same components or markup as the live site:

- **Home banners**: [HomePromoBanners](frontend/src/components/Home/PromoBanners.tsx) — same component used on the home page.
- **Featured category**: [FeaturedCategorySection](frontend/src/components/Home/FeaturedCategorySection.tsx) with placeholder products so layout and styling match; banner and slug come from form data.
- **Navbar**: [NavigationPreview](frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/Navigation/NavigationPreview.tsx) uses the same structure and classes as [PLPHeaderDesktopNav](frontend/src/components/PLP/Header/DesktopNav.tsx) (bg-stone-50, px-10 py-3, gap-6, same link styles).

## Panel editor style (hero-style collapsible panel)

The hero slider uses a collapsible side panel (320px, spring animation, rounded-xl border) for the slot editor. The same style is available on other customization pages:

- **CustomizationEditorPanel** ([frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/CustomizationEditorPanel.tsx](frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/CustomizationEditorPanel.tsx)) — Reusable collapsible panel: same width, motion, and chrome as the hero’s side panel.
- **CustomizationPreviewSection** — Optional `editorPanel` prop: when set, the section renders preview (left) + CustomizationEditorPanel (right) with a header toggle (PanelLeftClose / PanelRight).
- **UpsertPageContentWrapper** — Optional `usePanelLayout`: when `true` and `footer` is set, layout is preview (left) + form in CustomizationEditorPanel (right), with a bar that has the panel collapse toggle. Used by featured-category, home-banners, and navbar so the form lives in the hero-style panel.

## Key Files

- [frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/CustomizationPreviewSection.tsx](frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/CustomizationPreviewSection.tsx) — Section + viewport + optional browser frame + optional editor panel
- [frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/CustomizationEditorPanel.tsx](frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/CustomizationEditorPanel.tsx) — Hero-style collapsible side panel
- [frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/Navigation/NavigationPreview.tsx](frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/Navigation/NavigationPreview.tsx) — Navbar preview (same structure as PLPHeaderDesktopNav)
- [frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/TemplatePreview.tsx](frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/TemplatePreview.tsx) — Hero reference implementation

## Note on "N Issue(s)" in the status bar

The red "N Issue(s)" badge that sometimes appears at the bottom of the screen (e.g. in the editor status bar) comes from the IDE (Cursor/VS Code), not from the customization panel or the app. It reflects linter or TypeScript issues in the workspace and is unrelated to validation or errors inside the customization UI.
